  "query_preview": "..\n(Tomorrow through Sunday)\nIssued at 1233 PM CDT Sun Jul 5 2026\n\nA closed upper low will develop over northern Arkansas Monday,\nresulting in isolated mainly afternoon and early evening\nconvection from parts of southeast Oklahoma into western Arkansas.\nThis system will then move east of the area by Tuesday, with dry\nweather then expected through Thursday. After near normal\ntemperatures Monday and Tuesday, temperatures will warm above\nnormal by Wednesday and Thursday, and afternoon heat index values\nwill climb into the triple digits. The NBM still looks a bit\naggressive with the warming, and some downward trend in both\ndaytime and nighttime temperatures may occur in future forecasts\nfor Thursday and Friday. At least low rain chances will return\nThursday night into the first part of next weekend with the\napproach of a weak frontal boundary.",
